We are creating a portfolio website with a classical full-size page layout.

Pages:
Every route is a full-viewport page with a full-width content surface and one shared bottom navigation/header pill. Pages are navigated with ordinary links. There is no map canvas, camera pan, zoom, connector lines, top header, or right-side menu.

Architecture:
Multi-page site. Each URL loads its own HTML document with only that route’s content.
Routes: /, /about, /blog, /cases, /contacts, /cases/{slug}.
Browser Back/Forward work through normal document navigation.

Layout:
- Full-size content card filling the viewport width with natural document scrolling.
- One fixed bottom pill that blends identity, routes, theme, and the primary CTA.
  - Desktop: avatar + name, Home / About / Cases / Contacts, theme switch, Get in Touch.
  - Compact/mobile: collapsed pill with avatar, More, and Get in Touch; expanded state reveals routes and the theme switch above the action row.
- Back actions live in page content as the first block before the page heading/hero (not in the pill). About, Cases list, Contacts, Blog, and errors go Home; case details go to Cases.
- Blog stays reachable by URL but is hidden from the pill until content is ready.
- Elements scale proportionally with viewport size (rem + ui-scale tokens). Reserve bottom inset so content is never covered by the pill, including safe-area.

